     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is 850 mg three times daily. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas a different dose intended? These are common options:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day, which is the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily or about 567 mg three times daily. Tablet strengths come in 500, 850 and 1,000 mg, so 500 mg three times daily is more practical.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I can enter it with a note documenting the confirmation. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
